{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#3091","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#3091","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#3091\",\"parent_revision\":\"b8a566de91cb90dd4c68abb03cdb3593eafca96e41617d240720967b1c4b6dd8\",\"root_revision\":\"b8a566de91cb90dd4c68abb03cdb3593eafca96e41617d240720967b1c4b6dd8\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-20\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n`dh_paths.py`'s `compute_slug()` (used by `state_root()`, `backlog_dir`, `plan_dir`, `milestones_dir`, `research_dir`, `context_dir`, `reports_dir`) is `str(project_root).replace('/', '-')` \u2014 no `.lstrip('/')` \u2014 so the slug keeps its leading dash (e.g. `-home-user-repos-claude_skills`). But `backlog_core/server.py::_project_stub()` and `dh_core/operations.py::_dispatch_db_path()` each independently compute `str(project_root).lstrip('/').replace('/', '-')` \u2014 with lstrip, so that slug has no leading dash (e.g. `home-user-repos-claude_skills`).\\n\\nThis means `dispatch-state.db` currently lives in a sibling-but-different directory (`~/.dh/projects/home-user-repos-claude_skills/dispatch-state.db`) than every other Tier 2/3 state artifact (`~/.dh/projects/-home-user-repos-claude_skills/backlog/`, etc).\\n\\nDiscovered during #3062 research (`control-set.db` is required by ADR-3082-1 to nest under `dh_paths.state_root()`'s slug convention, prompting the comparison). Two independent local reimplementations of the same slug-computation logic diverging is itself worth fixing regardless of which convention is correct \u2014 there should be one slug function every caller uses.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **fix: dispatch-state.db path uses a different project-slug computation than dh_paths.state_root()** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Agent task - auto-derived from input\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-20\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"e6529ac039500d41bb173d4ce52e944d9f44d773e296e90e951fffd3e5d2dce4\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABP843Aw\"}"}